        "original_id": "0e7dfb07-11d9-579f-bec4-7f8b2944f143",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: André Jardin, Alexis de Tocqueville, Lydia Davis, Robert Hemenway\n- Works: Alexis de Tocqueville: 1805-1859, Tocqueville: A Biography, Democracy in America, De La Démocratie en Amérique\n- Topics: biography, translation, publication\n\nFacts:\n- Alexis de Tocqueville published De La Démocratie en Amérique in two volumes, with the first volume appearing in 1835 and the second in 1840.\n- De La Démocratie en Amérique is a classic French text by Alexis de Tocqueville.\n- André Jardin published the biography Alexis de Tocqueville: 1805-1859 in 1984.\n- Alexis de Tocqueville: 1805-1859 was translated into English as Tocqueville: A Biography in 1988 by Lydia Davis and Robert Hemenway.\n- André Jardin's 1984 biography was acclaimed as the definitive account of the life and career of Alexis de Tocqueville, the author of Democracy in America.",
